# GD-5 (round 19, writer 10): E §2 "`flows` over days before S is a hole whatever is dated there (HOLE-PRERUN,
# above)"; E §4.1 step 3 "dated outside [S, E]: kept for bindings, and after E for `flows` (`flows` over days before S
# is HOLE-PRERUN, §2)". gift[2025-12] is dated 2025-12-10, before S: flows over December 2025, and over a span from
# then into the run, are the hole `before the run's start`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
index mm = month 2025-11..2026-02
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

move gift[m in mm]: gifts
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  dom = 10
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask pre: flows(konto, 2025-12-01 .. 2025-12-31)
ask mix: flows(konto, 2025-12-01 .. 2026-01-31)
=== expect
mix: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-12-31
pre: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-12-31
